      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\n\nThe fixed angle $\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$ is in quadrant II with reference angle $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\qquad \\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$, then simplify the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin\\left(x+\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\sin x\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\cos x\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\cos x\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
